    "title": "'Totally Shocked' Chicago Police Officers Told to Stand Down When ICE Agents Surrounded by Mob of Protesters: Rep. Aaron Bean | NTD",
    "text": "Rep. Aaron Bean (R-Fla.) discussed with NTD's Steve Lance Chicago Mayor Brandon Johnson's accusation that President Donald Trump is escalating violence for deploying the National Guard, the Chicago Police being told to stand down while en route to help ICE agents who were surrounded by a mob of angry protestors on Saturday, and the bill he introduced, the Aviation Funding Stability Act of 2025, to ensure America’s air traffic controllers and essential Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) personnel will continue to be paid, even during a shutdown.\n'Totally Shocked' Chicago Police Officers Told to Stand Down When ICE Agents Surrounded by Mob of Protesters: Rep. Aaron Bean\nRep. Aaron Bean discussed with NTD's Steve Lance.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 10/8/2025, 11:59:29 PM EDT",
